  "description": "Child of C11-336. Contract: docs/markdown-viewer-design.md (binding). Builds against R1's bridge (Resources/markdown-viewer/BRIDGE.md) in parallel; lands after R1.\n\nScope: the native markdown panel on WKWebView, replacing MarkdownUI.\n\n- `MarkdownPanelView` hosts a WKWebView loading R1's bundle through a custom URL scheme handler (no file:// broad access); local images resolve only beside the open document (scoped read, no traversal outside what rendering needs); CSP blocks remote loads; JS from the document never runs; link clicks arrive over the bridge and route through c11 (http(s) \u2192 default browser or c11 browser per existing policy, relative .md \u2192 open in a markdown panel for now, anchors \u2192 in-page) and the web view's own navigation is cancelled. Record the panel's threat notes in docs/security-threat-model.md.\n- Weight: one shared WKProcessPool / configuration, lazy web view creation for panels never shown. Measure memory and creation time with 20 markdown panels in a tagged build (Atlas), compare with a tagged origin/main build, record both and the load average.\n- State model on MarkdownPanel: fontScale, theme, typeface, outlineOpen (explicit open/hide or nil = width default); per panel; last used in any panel becomes the new-panel default (extends markdown.fontScale.lastUsed); session snapshot carries theme, typeface and outline beside fontScale (SessionPersistence.swift, Workspace.swift restore); unknown/out-of-range/unreadable values fall back to the default for that field.\n- Existing paths keep working: `c11 markdown open`, live reload (file watch \u2192 push text, R1 re-renders changed blocks, scroll held), drop-to-open, session snapshot/restore, focus flash, pointer focus, the app-wide zoom keys through WorkspaceManager.zoomInFocusedMarkdown / zoomOutFocusedMarkdown / resetZoomFocusedMarkdown driving the markdown scale; WKWebView page zoom and magnification never intercept \u2318= / \u2318\u2212 / \u23180. Existing markdown tests stay green or get behavioural replacements. markdown.get_content keeps working.\n- Remove MarkdownUI (package dependency) and FencedCodeRenderer/MermaidRenderer's Mermaid path once nothing uses them.\n- Minimal interim chrome is fine (file name row); the full toolbar is R3.\n- No runModal on agent-reachable paths; socket threading and focus policy hold; dlog DEBUG-gated.\n\nProof: tagged Atlas build, markdown panel opens docs/c11-messaging-primitive-design.md offline with Mermaid; live reload mid-scroll without drift; restore after relaunch with non-default scale/theme/typeface; a malicious fixture (script tags, onerror, javascript: links, remote image) does nothing; the 20-panel numbers.",
  "done_at": "2026-10-08T15:33:05Z",
